\newlabel{fig:efficiencies}{{4}{13}{\textbf {The two control efficiencies and their resource dependence.} (a) Empirical information--response efficiency across the sensing--actuation grid. (b) Exact single-affinity thermodynamic efficiency $\eta _{\rm th}=hJ_c/(hJ_c+I_{\rm sens})$ as the actuation budget is varied for the three sensing budgets used experimentally. (c) Empirical sensing information, which rises strongly with $q_c$ without a proportional increase in controlled current}{figure.4}{}}
